# meta::sourceURL = https://www.wikihow.com/Grow-Beavertail-Cactus
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This guide explains how to grow Beavertail cactus, either from seeds in a shady garden in moist soil, leading to flowers in 4 years, or more quickly from cuttings, 6 months or older, cured in dry shade for 10-14 days, then planted upright in pots with drainage holes in the sun, watering after a month and letting soil dry, as well as fertilizing in spring, summer and fall.
# meta::summary2 = (human2) To grow the Beavertail Cactus, there are two primary methods, which include scattering the seeds in a shaded bed for slower growth or planting your own cuttings from a previously owned cactus in a soil and sand mixture and place in direct sunlight, while ensuring the roots are not oversaturated with water in the first month and that the cactus receives a balanced fertilizer.
# meta::summary3 = (human3) This guide explains two main methods for growing Beavertail Cactus: 1) scattering seeds in a shady bed, and 2) planting cuttings in a mix of soil and sand and ensuring sufficient water and lots of sun for faster results.
# meta::summary4 = (human4) The guide discusses two methods of growing Beavertail Cactus; the slower method is to purchase seeds and grow the cactus in a shady garden bed, and the faster method is to get Beavertail cactus cuttings and grow them in a pot with potting mix under plenty of sun.
# meta::summary5 = (human5) Using detailed instructions of two growth methods, this article describes how Beavertail Cacus can grow either by scattering purchased seeds in a shady garden bed and waiting 4 years, or by planting Beavertail cuttings in a mix of soil and sand and ensuring there is plenty of sunlight to grow quicker compared to planting seeds
# meta::title = How to Grow Beavertail Cactus
